	x: 0.8d,
	y: -0.4d,
	text: [
		"Items and machines in IndustrialCraft 2 are grouped into tiers based on the maximum EU it can output or receive per tick (EU/t).\n\nFor example, trying to power a Macerator (tier 1) with 128 EU/t (tier 2) will result in the Macerator exploding, destroying it.\nPowering a machine or storage unit with too much EU/t will result in the machine exploding.\n\nTransformer Upgrades can be used to increase the power tier of a machine by power tier per upgrade item. Different cables have different maximum allowed voltages and energy loss over distance.\n\n§6Voltage Tiers:§r\n1. LV (Low Voltage) - up to 32 EU/t (Tin Cable, Copper Cable)\n2. MV (Medium Voltage) - up to 128 EU/t (Copper Cable)\n3. HV (High Voltage) - up to 512 EU/t (Gold Cable)\n4. EV (Extreme Voltage) - up to 2048 EU/t (HV Cable)\n\nGlass Fibre Cable can handle up to 8192 EU/t with very low energy loss over distance.\n\nIt is also possible to use Mekanism Universal Cables to transfer EU without worrying about voltage tiers."
	],
